uote proper ones that will lead  the navy on the right path once the  world government is taken down an  absolutely fantastic supporting  character that is written very  unconventionally but that i absolutely  have grown to love so where does our  pink-haired bad boy go from here the  abolishment of the shichibukai system  was one of the major outcomes of the  reverie and threw a lot of heavy hitters  back into the game i can tell you how  excited i am to see where mihawk is  going to end up buggy is surely gonna  run into luffy again at some point as  well but the most interesting storyline  right now is undoubtedly boa hancock's  confrontation with kobe  [Music]  the scared kid from the east blue versus  the revered pirate empress now the  outcome of this battle is heavily  debated after all both are pretty damn  powerful kobe has shown us how much  stronger he has gotten while hancock is  even able to use congress hockey but of  course the only thing that combines this  unlikely duo is their love for luffy  hancock is the self-declared future wife  of the pirate king while kobe is the  biggest member of the luffy fan club  second only to barcelona  i am more than curious to see how this  fight is going to turn out but i'm  convinced that sooner or later both of  them will realize that they're actually  on the same side on luffy's side and i  don't put it past either of them to team  up and come for luffy's aid maybe even  still in wano however what i think is  even more fun to think and speculate  about is whether kobe will actually  fulfill his big dream and become a  marine admiral by the end of the story  and there's actually a super interesting  theory about this that exists in a  number of different variations and with  different twists so it's kind of hard to  figure out who took credit for this  originally nonetheless it's incredibly  fun and makes surprisingly much sense i  feel now as i premise for this theory we  of course have to assume that kobe will 